<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Tiger Oats year shr up 25 percent.</title>
<headline>Tiger Oats year shr up 25 percent.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     372.2	 vs 297.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 132.0	 vs 108.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   792.8	 vs 494.7</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   1,282.4     vs 836.5</p>
<p>    Tax			 374.6	 vs 267.7</p>
<p>    Interest received     24.9	  vs 15.1 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		  13,630.0    vs 11,978.7</p>
<p>    Abnormal gains	  230.6	 vs 13.7</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  21.0	  vs 4.6</p>
<p>Attrib to outside</p>
<p>    shareholders	    136.0	 vs 78.7</p>
<p>Div payable January 7</p>
<p>on register December 17</p>
<p>Full name: Tiger Oats Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts forecast diversified foods group Tiger Oat's earnings before exceptionals at between 344 and 351 cents a share, with a consensus of 348.3. The dividend was seen on a range of 122-124 cents.</p>
<p>The abnormal gain reflects change of interest in susidiaries, associates and other investments.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
